{{also|copout|cop-out}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{m|en|cop a plea}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|cops out|copping out|copped out}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[avoid]] or [[shirk]], either by failing to perform, or by performing in a grossly [[insufficient]], [[negligent]], or [[superficial]] manner.
#: ''Faced with the prospect of cooking for himself, his first thought was to '''cop out''' and order a pizza.''
# To [[plead]] [[guilty]] and ask for [[mercy]].

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|cop-out}}

====Synonyms====
* [[weasel out]]

